            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This was already suggested in #646 and #760. Following [example for making a mapping that creates a split](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e736fe131e6c18d39eecffb43d582c3e95550a90/doc/mini-files.txt#L433-L462) is the suggest approach here. Note, that examples only create a split and changes target window to be that split. Follow with actually opening a file the usual way (`l` or `L` by default).",
