        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It seems the suggested approach doesn't work anymore. It creates the split but doesn't open the selected file.\r\n\r\nThe suggested linked approach ([this example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7b4d5d48b6b5a75009d63f8f3e4ef4819b7e8139/doc/mini-files.txt#L477-L502)) only makes split and keeps explorer opened. The provided code differs from the example by the `vim.defer_fn()` call inside `map_split`. It explicitly tells to change target window and *close the explorer*, which is exactly what happens.\r\n\r\nAdd the `MiniFiles.go_in()` call before closing and it should open the file under cursor.",
